<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>
  <!-- EN: An anchor is a marked area inside a piece where something happens once the piece is placed.\n\nConnect anchors tie the piece to its surroundings. Wall is where the town wall docks, Outside tells which side faces out, Annex is where annexes attach.\n\nLoot anchors place objects from an object list and fill them from a loot table. Object anchors place objects from an object list with a chance, without loot. Pawn anchors bring in people or animals from a pawn list, with a role that decides whether they stay and fight or run.\n\nAn anchor whose list does not exist marks the piece red in the editor. -->
  <CBF_Help_Anchors.description>錨點是部件中標記的區域，部件落地時在其處發生某事。\n\n連線錨點把部件與其環境相連。Wall是城牆對接處，Outside指明朝外一側，Annex是附屬建築的位置。\n\n戰利品錨點放置物件清單的物品並按戰利品表填充。物件錨點按機率放置物件清單的物品，無戰利品。角色錨點從單位清單帶來人或動物，帶決定其留守作戰或逃跑的角色。\n\n錨點引用不存在的清單時，編輯器將該部件標紅。</CBF_Help_Anchors.description>
  <!-- EN: Anchors -->
  <CBF_Help_Anchors.label>錨點</CBF_Help_Anchors.label>
  <!-- EN: An annex is a small piece that attaches to a house: a stable, a woodshed, a beer garden. Everything about it is data in the categories and pieces, nothing is fixed in code.\n\nAnnex categories on the house's category say which annexes may attach to it. An empty list takes the list of the parent category.\n\nChance per anchor is the chance that an annex is built at one annex anchor of the house, default 0.6. At most caps the number of annexes per house, default 2.\n\nRepeatable belongs on the category of the annex itself. Yes allows the same annex several times on one house.\n\nWeight decides which annex is picked when several fit. For annexes, a weight below 1 is also the chance that this annex is tried at all.\n\nThe anchor is a Connect anchor named Annex. On the house it lies on the outer wall. On the annex it lies either on its outer wall, when both share that wall, or one cell outside its shape, when the annex only touches the house. -->
  <CBF_Help_Annexes.description>附屬建築是附加到房屋的小部件：馬廄、柴棚、啤酒花園。一切均為類別與部件中的資料，無程式碼固定。\n\n房屋類別上的附屬建築類別說明允許哪些附屬建築。空清單繼承父級類別。\n\n每錨點機率是房屋附屬錨點上生成附屬建築的機率，預設0.6。每棟房屋的附屬建築數量有上限，預設2。\n\nMultiple設在附屬建築類別上，允許同一附屬建築多次附加到同一房屋。\n\n權重決定多個適配時選哪個。附屬建築的權重小於1時也是嘗試機率。\n\n錨點是名為Annex的連線錨點。在房屋中位於外牆，在附屬建築中位於兩者共牆處，或形狀外一格（若僅毗鄰）。</CBF_Help_Annexes.description>
  <!-- EN: Annexes -->
  <CBF_Help_Annexes.label>附屬建築</CBF_Help_Annexes.label>
  <!-- EN: A district is a building programme. It says what the generator should put into this ward and how much of it.\n\nEach line is either a category (Workshop, HouseSmall) or one specific piece (Workshop_Baker). Min and max bound how many of them are built. Weight decides how often a piece is drawn when several fit the same category.\n\nA piece listed under a category counts towards that category's limit. That is why the Baker sits indented under Workshop instead of standing next to it.\n\nCrop plots and animal pens belong to a district too. That is how the generator knows a farmstead gets fields and a tavern does not. -->
  <CBF_Help_Districts.description>一個區是一份建造計劃。它規定生成器應在此區劃中放置什麼、各多少。\n\n每一行是一個類別（Workshop、HouseSmall）或一個特定部件（Workshop_Baker）。Min與Max限制生成數量。多個部件適配同一類別時，權重決定抽取頻率。\n\n列在類別下的部件計入該類別上限。因此麵包師縮排排在Workshop下，而非並排。\n\n農田與畜欄也屬於一個區。這樣生成器知道農莊要農田，而酒館不要。</CBF_Help_Districts.description>
  <!-- EN: Districts -->
  <CBF_Help_Districts.label>區</CBF_Help_Districts.label>
  <!-- EN: Towers and other defensive works that sit in the wall ring.\n\nThe generator spaces them along the wall by itself, at the corners first and then along the long straight runs. How many fit follows from the length of the wall, not from a number you set here.\n\nThe size of the largest tower in this list also sets how much room the planner reserves at every corner, so a very large tower makes the whole outline coarser. -->
  <CBF_Help_Emplacements.description>嵌入城牆環的塔樓與其他防禦建築。\n\n生成器自行沿城牆分佈，先角、後長直段。數量由城牆長度決定，而非此處數字。\n\n清單中最大塔樓也決定規劃器在各角留出的空間。非常大的塔樓會使整個輪廓更粗糙。</CBF_Help_Emplacements.description>
  <!-- EN: Field emplacements -->
  <CBF_Help_Emplacements.label>防禦陣地</CBF_Help_Emplacements.label>
  <!-- EN: Which of your settlement plans are used when the player walks into a base of this faction.\n\nThe assignment is not stored on the faction. It is stored as factionTags inside the plan, and the generator collects every plan whose tags match the faction. Two mods can therefore both serve the same faction without either one overwriting the other.\n\nA plan that names no faction at all serves every faction. That is why a fresh plan shows up everywhere until you assign it.\n\nRemoving works only for plans attached by faction name. A plan attached through the faction category has to be detached in the plan itself. -->
  <CBF_Help_Factions.description>玩家進入某派系基地時，你的哪些據點型別被採用。\n\n關聯在計劃的factionTags，而非派系。生成器收集每個標籤匹配的據點計劃。兩個模組可以服務同一派系而不互相覆蓋。\n\n未指名派系的計劃適用於所有派系。因此新計劃到處出現，直到你為其關聯派系。\n\n只能透過派系名稱關聯移除。透過派系類別關聯的計劃需在計劃本身解除。</CBF_Help_Factions.description>
  <!-- EN: Settlement plans per faction -->
  <CBF_Help_Factions.label>每派系據點</CBF_Help_Factions.label>
  <!-- EN: Where a road crosses the wall, a gatehouse is built.\n\nThe number follows from the roads, not from a setting. The planner lays out the approach roads first and puts a gate wherever one has to pass through the ring, then checks that every gate can actually be reached from outside.\n\nA piece used here needs a passable opening. Without one the ward is sealed and the whole layout is discarded. -->
  <CBF_Help_Gatehouses.description>道路穿過城牆處生成門樓。\n\n數量由道路決定，而非設定。規劃器先鋪設通道，凡穿越城牆環處設門，再檢查每座門從外部可達。\n\n此處部件必須有可通行的開口。沒有它區劃即封閉，整個設計被廢棄。</CBF_Help_Gatehouses.description>
  <!-- EN: Gatehouses -->
  <CBF_Help_Gatehouses.label>門樓</CBF_Help_Gatehouses.label>
  <!-- EN: Crop plots and animal pens for the open countryside.\n\nA crop plot is grown around a rural building, not dropped on the map at random. Which buildings get one is decided by the district the plot is listed under. Min and max bound how many plots that building may have.\n\nA pen holds one kind of animal, drawn from a unit list. The herd size is the second row, indented under the pen.\n\nBoth get a fence with one gate. Where rock or water already closes the line, no fence is built in front of it. -->
  <CBF_Help_Rural.description>開闊鄉野的農田與畜欄。\n\n農田圍繞鄉間建築生長，不隨機放置。哪些建築獲得農田由農田所屬的區決定。Min與Max限制此建築可擁有的農田數。\n\n畜欄圈養單位清單中的一種動物。畜群大小在第二行，縮排排在畜欄下。\n\n兩者都有帶門的圍欄。岩石或水面已封閉處不建圍欄。</CBF_Help_Rural.description>
  <!-- EN: Farmland -->
  <CBF_Help_Rural.label>農田與畜欄</CBF_Help_Rural.label>
  <!-- EN: Nothing you assign here shows up until RimWorld actually hands faction bases to this generator. That is what the takeover switch does.\n\nIt writes one patch file into the Patches folder of the current mod. The patch swaps a single generation step, Settlement for CBF_Settlement, and leaves everything else in place, so faction bases keep their rocks and their power lines.\n\nIf a patch file is already there, the operation is added to it and the rest of the file is kept. Switching the takeover off removes only that operation, not the file, unless nothing else is left in it.\n\nA faction with no matching plan falls back to RimWorld's own settlement, never to an empty map. -->
  <CBF_Help_Takeover.description>此處分配的內容只有在RimWorld把派系基地交給此生成器後才出現——正是"接管"開關所為。\n\n它向所選模組的Patches目錄寫入補丁檔案。補丁替換地圖生成的一個步驟（Settlement換成CBF_Settlement），其餘保持不變。派系基地因此保留其岩石與電纜。\n\n已存在補丁檔案時，僅追加該操作，檔案其餘部分保留。關閉僅移除該操作，而非檔案，除非檔案中無其他內容。\n\n沒有匹配計劃的派系得到RimWorld自己的據點，絕不生成空白地圖。</CBF_Help_Takeover.description>
  <!-- EN: Takeover -->
  <CBF_Help_Takeover.label>接管</CBF_Help_Takeover.label>
  <!-- EN: How much a piece wants to stand against the town wall. The planner reads it when it places buildings.\n\nForbidden keeps the piece away from the wall. Avoid, Allowed, Preferred and Strongly preferred weigh the spots along the wall lower or higher. Required forces contact: the piece is only placed where it touches the wall.\n\nA piece without a value of its own takes the wall contact of its category. Yes there means Preferred. -->
  <CBF_Help_WallContact.description>部件希望貼靠城鎮城牆的程度。規劃器放置建築時讀取。\n\n禁止使部件遠離城牆。迴避、允許、偏好與強烈偏好對牆邊位置加權。必須強制接觸：僅在接觸城牆處放置部件。\n\n無自有值的部件繼承其類別的貼牆程度。類別中的"是"表示偏好。</CBF_Help_WallContact.description>
  <!-- EN: At the wall -->
  <CBF_Help_WallContact.label>貼牆</CBF_Help_WallContact.label>
  <!-- EN: The wall pieces this ward is built from. The generator picks from the list whenever it needs a stretch of wall, so several entries give a wall that varies along its length.\n\nDepth is how thick the ring is. One is a palisade, three is a town wall with a rampart walk on top.\n\nWhere a mountain meets the line, the mountain is the wall and nothing is built in front of it. -->
  <CBF_Help_Walls.description>構築此區劃的城牆部件。需要城牆段時生成器從清單選取。多個條目構成沿其長度變化的城牆。\n\n深度是環的厚度。1是木柵欄，3是帶步道的城牆。\n\n岩石碰到城牆線時以岩石為牆，其前不建造。</CBF_Help_Walls.description>
  <!-- EN: Walls -->
  <CBF_Help_Walls.label>城牆</CBF_Help_Walls.label>
  <!-- EN: The door that closes the passages through this ward's wall, for example a wooden door for a palisade.\n\nEmpty uses the door of the material list of the settlement type, which is what most wards want. The gatehouse is something else, it is set under Fortification. -->
  <CBF_Help_WardGate.description>封閉此區劃城牆通道的門，例如木柵欄配木門。\n\n留空從材料清單取門，多數區劃想要這樣。門樓是另一回事，設在防禦陣地之下。</CBF_Help_WardGate.description>
  <!-- EN: Ward door -->
  <CBF_Help_WardGate.label>區劃大門</CBF_Help_WardGate.label>
  <!-- EN: A ward is one ring of the settlement. A market town has three: the old town behind the high wall, the suburb behind a lighter one, and the open countryside around them.\n\nEverything else hangs off a ward. Its wall, its towers, its gatehouses, and the districts that decide what gets built inside it.\n\nThe order in the list is the order from the middle outwards. The innermost ward is the one the generator protects best and fills first, so put what matters there. -->
  <CBF_Help_Wards.description>一個區劃是據點的一環。一座集鎮有三個：高牆後的老城、較矮城牆後的近郊，以及環繞它們的開闊鄉野。\n\n其餘一切從區劃衍生：其城牆、塔樓、門樓，以及決定內部建造內容的區。\n\n清單中順序由內而外。最內層區劃是生成器保護最好、最先填滿的，把重要的東西放在那裡。</CBF_Help_Wards.description>
  <!-- EN: Wards -->
  <CBF_Help_Wards.label>區劃</CBF_Help_Wards.label>
</LanguageData>
